KZ3 patch 1089 (SPU pass 67): the common exponent-255 lanes of fa/fs/fm (patches 1071/1079) resolved inline inside
the unlikely branch, without the call to spu__xr_fixv: an exponent-0 operand (fm -> +0, fa/fs -> the other word),
fm products >= 2^129 (biased exponents summing to >= 383 -> sign | Smax), fa/fs operands more than 28 exponents apart
(the larger word, minus one unit when the signs differ, +0 at exponent 0). These are the K4 probe's top cases (0 *
frest(0), Smax + x, Smax * Smax, 0 - 0xFFFFFFFF). Other lanes still go to spu__xr_fixv; the hot path is unchanged.
Bit-identical to the 1071 lane forms (tools/spu/test_spu_xr.c check_1089). KZ3_SPU_XRQ=0 keeps the old path.

